      "heading": "Water ionises itself",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Even pure water has a few ions. One water passes a proton to another.",
          "write": "H₂O + H₂O ⇌ H₃O⁺ + OH⁻"
        },
        {
          "say": "In pure water at 25 degrees, both are 1.0 times 10 to the minus 7.",
          "write": "[H₃O⁺] = [OH⁻] = 1.0 × 10⁻⁷ M"
        },
        {
          "say": "Their product is always 1.00 times 10 to the minus 14. This is K w.",
          "write": "Kw = [H₃O⁺][OH⁻] = 1.00 × 10⁻¹⁴",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 280,
